{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/vqt83el4","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":64,"top":145,"width":1150,"height":100},"text":"Ghost: active in 3 of the first 4 Autumn weeks, then a weekly average\nbelow 10% of the early average. Include weeks with zero activity.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":27,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#E6ECEF","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/upk7u9kj","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":64,"top":270,"width":1150,"height":100},"text":"Vampire: more than 21 night-active dates and more night than day dates.\nNight is after midnight through 05:00 UTC inclusive.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":27,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#E6ECEF","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/5gbq9o36","slideIndex":1,"position":{"left":64,"top":395,"width":1150,"height":100},"text":"Werewolf: at least two robust weekly spikes in each of Autumn and Spring.\nSpike size is an exploratory choice, not specified in the guide.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":27,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#FFA54C","alignment":"left"}}
